      "shortName": "viewnode-task-4-retire-root-ha",
      "title": "viewnode-task-4 retire root HANDOFF and fix stale Modal reference",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Retire the root `HANDOFF.md` (the planner + `.planner/HANDOFF.md` are the handoff mechanism now) and fix the one stale claim it flagged.\n\n## 1. Delete `HANDOFF.md` from the repo root\nEverything in it is either **done and merged**, or **rescued into the planner** (verified before deletion):\n- §1a–1h (Modal removal, `Base.focusable`, Button disabled/Secondary styling, overlay-capture policy, text-field uppercase, confirm dialog + random pane names, `Glyph::CaretUp`, the AGENTS.md ⭐ block) — **all shipped**, on `main` or PR #237.\n- §2 accelerator decisions + §3b — **rescued into the planner phase `button-shortcut`** (`402d22d4`) description, which is now marked UNBLOCKED on the Button side.\n- §3a (ViewNode → all widgets) — **done/superseded**: `viewnode-task-2`/`-3` shipped (PR #237), and `viewnode-task-1` was replaced by the phase `viewnode-choice` (`1df9c36c`, 8 tasks).\n- §3c leftovers — **rescued as tasks**: Dialog font-derived min-width → `gridui-07` task `bd6b5935`; context-menu keyboard nav bug → `context-menu` task `bc9ca992`; the stale `Modal` reference → this task.\n\n## 2. Fix the stale `Modal` in AGENTS.md\nThe ⛔ STOP list (~line 20) still names `Modal` in \"Widgets available today\": `…Label, Input, Select, Modal, CommandPalette, Toast, Tabs, Pane, …`. The **`Modal` widget was deleted** (superseded by `Dialog`; the app builds a `Dialog` from `ModalSpec` via `OverlayHost::open_modal`). Advertising a widget that no longer exists sends the next agent looking for it. Replace `Modal` with `Dialog` in that list.\n\nNB: the app-side types `ModalSpec` / `ModalResult` / `ModalAction` and the `Modal` **layer band** are still real — only the *widget* is gone. Don't over-correct.\n\n## Gates\nNo code change; `cargo test -p heca-grid-ui -p heca` unaffected. Commit with the docs.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-13 — commit `db1d2c1`, pushed to `feat/viewnode-button-composition` (PR #237).\n\n## 1. Root `HANDOFF.md` DELETED\nAudited line by line before deleting. Nothing was lost:\n- **§1a–1h** (Modal widget removal, `Base.focusable` centralization, Button disabled + Secondary theme-consistency, overlay-capture interaction policy, text-field uppercase fix, confirm dialog + random-pane-name removal, `Glyph::CaretUp`, the AGENTS.md ⭐ block) — **all shipped**, on `main` or PR #237.\n- **§2 + §3b (the accelerator design)** — **rescued into the planner phase `button-shortcut` (`402d22d4`)**, whose description now carries the locked decisions verbatim: trigger is **`Ctrl+<letter>`** (works in confirm AND form dialogs — a bare letter collides with typing); rendered **INSIDE** the button as a **composed `Icon + Label` child** (never hand-drawn, never adjacent); Button self-submits, `FocusManager::deliver_accelerator` reaches a non-focused button; `ModalAction.shortcut: Option<char>` set by the confirm builder with **semantic** letters (`n` = cancel, `y` = proceed — a widget cannot infer that \"Cancel\" means \"No\"); the glyph is **NerdFont**, not Phosphor (`Glyph::CaretUp` **stays in the enum** per the user's keep-directive, but is not used for this). The phase is now marked **UNBLOCKED on the Button side** — this session's composition refactor is exactly what it was waiting for; it still needs `gridui-03` (NerdFont).\n- **§3a** (ViewNode → all widgets) — **done/superseded**: `viewnode-task-2` + `-3` shipped (PR #237); `viewnode-task-1` was canceled and replaced by the phase **`viewnode-choice`** (`1df9c36c`, 8 tasks).\n- **§3c leftovers** — **rescued as real tasks**: Dialog font-derived min-width (needs `Style::min_width`, which does not exist) → `gridui-07` task **`bd6b5935`**; context-menu keyboard-nav bug (Ctrl+j/k + arrows don't move the highlight; the code path *traces* correct, so it **needs a runtime repro**, not another trace) → `context-menu` task **`bc9ca992`**; the stale `Modal` reference → this task.\n\n## 2. AGENTS.md stale `Modal` FIXED\nThe ⛔ STOP list advertised a **`Modal` widget that no longer exists** (deleted, superseded by `Dialog`) — the next agent would have gone looking for it. Replaced with `Dialog`, added `Choice`, and added an explicit note that the app-side `ModalSpec` / `ModalResult` / `ModalAction` types and the `Modal` layer **band** are still real (so nobody over-corrects and rips those out).\n\n## Gates\nDocs-only; no code touched. Workspace unaffected.",
