    {
      "id": "db61a57c-fccf-4a50-b2bf-fe23a5b7ae7f",
      "phaseId": "1df9c36c-5c29-4288-9fe1-7a6e9c72179b",
      "number": 289,
      "shortId": "CYGDN",
      "priority": 9,
      "shortName": "label-decorations-italic-under",
      "title": "label decorations italic underline strikethrough",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Requested by the user (2026-07-14) after reviewing the showcase: `Label` exposed only `bold`. Added **italic**, **underline** and **strikethrough**.\n\n## DONE 2026-07-14 — user tested and approved. heca 349 · heca-grid-ui 142, clippy clean.\n\n## The design — the four attributes split in two, and the split is the point\n- **`bold` / `italic` are FONT attributes** — the shaper picks the glyphs.\n  - `bold` → the embedded family's real bold face.\n  - `italic` → a **synthesized oblique** (glyph shear, `faux_italic`), **not** `Style::Italic`. Geist Mono ships **no italic face** (`heca-grid-ui/src/font.rs`), so a real italic request would either render upright or substitute a **proportional** fallback — and a proportional fallback breaks the monospace advances every measure in the library assumes (`chars × font × MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO`). The shear keeps the same face and widths. **The renderer already had this** (`TextCommand.faux_italic`, `text.rs:1087`); grid-ui simply never carried the flag. Reason is written at the mapping point in `queue_text_in_box`.\n- **`underline` / `strikethrough` are DECORATIONS** (the user's call) — a line is not a glyph, it is a rect. `Label` draws them itself. **This is why underline cost zero renderer change.**\n\n## API shape\n- `Label`: `.italic(bool)` / `.underline(bool)` / `.strikethrough(bool)` + `italic_signal()` / `underline_signal()` / `strikethrough_signal()`. All four attributes are `Signal<bool>` (matching `bold`, which is one because `Item` drives it): a parent restyles **in place**, no rebuild — a link underlining on hover, a row striking its label through when done.\n- **`PaintCx::text`'s trailing `bold: bool` became a `TextStyle` value** (`{ bold, italic }`; `REGULAR` / `BOLD` / `ITALIC` + chainable `.bold(is_active)`). 21 call sites moved over (mechanical). The point: the **next** text attribute won't break the signature again. `TextCmd.bold` → `TextCmd.style`; `TextStyle` exported from the root + prelude.\n- Decorations are painted in the label's **resolved** color (own → inherited content color → theme foreground), so a decorated label inside a `Button` tints with its hover/disabled state for free.\n- Geometry is font-relative (no pixel constants): thickness `font × 0.07` floored at 1px; underline `0.42 × font` below the run's centre; strike `0.06 × font` above it (a line through the exact middle reads low, since lowercase mass sits above the box centre).\n- **Decorations follow the text RUN, not the box** — a container can widen a child's bounds (a `Select` does exactly that to its option rows) and `align` then decides where the run sits, so a rule spanning the box would be mostly empty line. `run_rect()` resolves it.\n\n## Tests (+2 heca-grid-ui → 142, +1 heca → 349)\n`label_weight_and_slant_are_font_attributes_decorations_are_rects` (weight+slant reach the shaper as `TextStyle` on the run and emit **no** rects; a decoration emits a rect and leaves the run `REGULAR`; underline below the centre, strike above; both → two rules; thickness ≥ 1px; an **empty** label draws nothing) · `label_decorations_follow_the_text_run_not_the_box` (widen the bounds the way a container does, `End`-aligned: the rule is run-width and sits at the right edge) · `label_text_attributes_are_authorable` (declarative: props → font attrs on the run + the strike as a rect).\n\n## Also\n- `realize`: `Label` props `bold` / `italic` / `underline` / `strikethrough` (Bool, default false). Signals are deliberately **not** declarative — a `ViewNode` is static data and cannot carry a live signal (same rule as host-only `ScrollBar`).\n- Showcase: a **Label** row (above Input) — REGULAR · BOLD · ITALIC · UNDERLINE · STRIKETHROUGH · ALL FOUR.\n- Docs: `docs/widgets.md` `Label` entry rewritten — the font-vs-decoration table with the *why*, the geometry table, the run-not-box rule, native examples (each attribute, combined, and both signal-driven idioms) and the declarative form; the `PaintCx` table row for `.text(.., TextStyle)`; the model table. Rustdoc: module-level explanation on `label.rs`, `TextStyle` on `scene.rs`.\n\n## Not done (offered, user deferred)\nTruncation/ellipsis (a long label currently overflows its box), wrapping / multi-line, letter-spacing, case transforms. Truncation is the load-bearing one — several widgets would want it.\n\n## Gates\nclippy 0 warnings · heca **349** · heca-grid-ui **142** + 71 + 1 · showcase builds. No `cargo fmt`.",
